docs/DEPLOYMENT.md :: disproven :: The first unattended run reads in `journalctl -u apt-daily-upgrade` and `/var/log/unattended-upgrades/unattended-upgrades.log` (root). No apt timer has a stamp under `/var/lib/systemd/timers/` (measured 2026-11-05), so `Persistent=true` has no missed run to catch up: enabling fires nothing, and the first run is the next 13:00. **To go back to `scheduled`:** `sudo systemctl disable --now` and `mask` both timers, remove `processor-periodic`, and set the knob's `posture`.
